many came together to raise funds for  the family of a father and son  killed in a wrong way crash our team has  been covering this story since it  happened in late may on the u.s 95 near  rancho  reporter kate houston joins us live in  the newsroom with more on the efforts to  help this family left behind  kate yes sasha it's been a little over  two weeks now since the robledos lost  two beloved members of their family they  tell me they're heartbroken  but they're so grateful for the support  that they've received so far  and that support continued today with a  community car wash hosted by the los  villanos booster club  the president of the club tells me they  wanted to help because this tragedy  could have happened to anybody  around a dozen people came out to scrub  down some cars and take donations  those will go directly to the families  of porfirio and rodolfo robledo  eloisa the mother and wife of the  victims say they're still in shock  my husband was dedicated to work to his  sons  he had a lot of dreams to see more  family like my daughter  and his grandkids my son was a very hard  working man  he was very responsible and is leaving  behind his four kids and wife  who are in mexico police say the driver  who hit the robleros was impaired  eloise is now asking the community to be  aware of their actions  saying innocent people are paying the  price the money raised at today's  fundraiser will go to the family  and will help cover funeral expenses  donations are also being taken through  zell and a gofundme all of that  information can be found on our website  8newsnow.com  back to you sasha
 

